+# EPMCDME-14452: LiteLLM Virtual Key Model Enforcement Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** When a project's `allowed_models` field is saved, regenerate all three per-category virtual keys with the updated model list so LiteLLM enforces model narrowing on API calls.
+
+**Architecture:** Wire the PATCH `/projects/{projectName}/allowed-models` endpoint (completed in ticket 14452-A) to trigger key regeneration via the existing LiteLLM adapter infrastructure. Pass the project's `allowed_models` value through the service layer to the adapter's `_recreate_project_budget_key_alias()` method. When `allowed_models` is NULL, regenerate with `models=None` (no restriction).
+
+**Tech Stack:** FastAPI (router), SQLModel (ORM), PostgreSQL (array storage), LiteLLM (virtual key metadata), pytest (testing)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Tests MUST run inside Docker container (see CLAUDE.md Testing Protocol)
+- All code must follow `.ai-run/guides/` patterns (layered architecture, error handling, logging)
+- Virtual keys for a project must all receive identical `models` lists (no per-category variance)
+- NULL `allowed_models` means `models=None` in key metadata (no narrowing)
+- Non-empty list must be validated (empty lists rejected)
